  "details": "Currently you’re able to adjust the Third Person camera position in the game settings (Settings > Graphics > Basic). However, they are global for every avatar so while some avatars look good with certain camera positioning, some may require the settings be readjusted (from my current experience I found that shorter more cartoonish avatars like some Pokémon for example, require camera position adjustments). Having to manually do this every time you change avatar can get annoying.\n\nSo my request is to add a Third Person camera position setting in the Expressions Menu (where the avatar height option is). So that every avatar can have its own unique Third Person camera position.\n\nThis setting should have the same settings as the global Third Person camera settings, as well as a reset button to revert it back to the global settings.",
